---
import { ThemeToggle } from '@/components/theme-toggle'
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/main.astro'
---

<MainLayout
  description="Learn how to choose a template, enter content, and download Open Graph images with Nore OG."
  title="How to use · Nore OG">
  <header class="border-b">
    <nav
      aria-label="Main navigation"
      class="mx-auto flex h-14 w-full max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-4">
      <a class="flex items-center gap-2.5" href="/">
        <img
          alt="Nore OG"
          class="size-7 rounded-md"
          height="28"
          src="/logo/logo.svg"
          width="28"
        />
        <span class="hidden text-sm font-medium sm:inline">Nore OG</span>
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-1 text-xs">
        <a
          class="rounded-md px-2.5 py-1.5 text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted hover:text-foreground"
          href="/">
          Home
        </a>
        <a
          aria-current="page"
          class="rounded-md px-2.5 py-1.5 font-medium"
          href="/how">
          How to use
        </a>
        <a
          class="rounded-md px-2.5 py-1.5 text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted hover:text-foreground"
          href="/self-host">
          Self-host
        </a>
        <a
          class="rounded-md px-2.5 py-1.5 text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted hover:text-foreground"
          href="/zh/how">
          中文
        </a>
        <ThemeToggle locale="en-US" />
      </div>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">HOW TO USE</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
        Generate share images with Nore OG
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        The workbench renders only the currently selected template. Start with a
        content preset, then adjust each field for your page.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="mt-12 divide-y border-y">
      <li class="grid gap-4 py-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-sm font-medium">Choose a template</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            On desktop, scroll through the template rail on the left. On a narrow
            screen, select the current template or “All templates” to open the full
            picker.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid gap-4 py-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-sm font-medium">Apply a content preset</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            A preset fills the title, description, brand, author, date, and logo at
            once, making it easy to test different content lengths.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid gap-4 py-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-sm font-medium">Edit manually</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Expand “Edit manually” to change any field. Enter one author per line for
            multiple authors. A custom logo requires a public URL.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid gap-4 py-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">04</span>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-sm font-medium">Render and download</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Select “Update preview” to confirm the final result, then download a
            scalable SVG or a publication-ready PNG.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <section class="mt-20 scroll-mt-8" id="api">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">API</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
          Generate images from a website or application
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
          Replace the example domain with your Nore OG API address. Use the GET
          endpoint directly as an image URL, or use the POST endpoint to generate and
          save files from a server.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border bg-card">
        <div class="border-b px-4 py-3">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-medium">Use a URL</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-5 text-muted-foreground">
            Call <code class="font-mono text-foreground">/render.svg</code> or <code
              class="font-mono text-foreground">/render.png</code
            > and pass the template and content as query parameters.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre
          class="overflow-x-auto bg-muted/50 p-4 text-xs leading-5"><code>{`curl --get 'https://og.example.com/render.svg' \\
  --data-urlencode 'template=nore-minimal' \\
  --data-urlencode 'title=Designing reliable Open Graph images' \\
  --data-urlencode 'description=Generated with Nore OG' \\
  --output open-graph.svg`}</code></pre>
        <div class="border-t px-4 py-3">
          <p class="text-xs leading-5 text-muted-foreground">
            To publish the result on a webpage, use the PNG endpoint directly in an
            Open Graph tag:
          </p>
          <pre
            class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border bg-background p-3 text-xs leading-5"><code>{`<meta
  property="og:image"
  content="https://og.example.com/render.png?template=nore-minimal&title=Your%20title"
/>`}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border bg-card">
        <div class="border-b px-4 py-3">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-medium">Use JSON</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-5 text-muted-foreground">
            Send JSON to <code class="font-mono text-foreground">/api/render</code>
            and use <code class="font-mono text-foreground">format</code> to select SVG
            or PNG.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre
          class="overflow-x-auto bg-muted/50 p-4 text-xs leading-5"><code>{`curl 'https://og.example.com/api/render' \\
  --request POST \\
  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  --data '{
    "format": "svg",
    "template": "nore-minimal",
    "title": "Designing reliable Open Graph images",
    "description": "Generated with Nore OG"
  }' \\
  --output open-graph.svg`}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border bg-card px-4 py-3">
        <h3 class="text-xs font-medium">Available fields and authentication</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-muted-foreground">
          The render API supports <code class="font-mono text-foreground"
            >template</code
          >, <code class="font-mono text-foreground">title</code>, <code
            class="font-mono text-foreground">description</code
          >, <code class="font-mono text-foreground">author</code>, <code
            class="font-mono text-foreground">date</code
          >, <code class="font-mono text-foreground">brandName</code>, <code
            class="font-mono text-foreground">logoId</code
          >, and <code class="font-mono text-foreground">logoUrl</code>. If your
          deployment sets <code class="font-mono text-foreground"
            >OG_INTERNAL_TOKEN</code
          >, requests must also include <code class="font-mono text-foreground"
            >Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code
          >. If the URL will be used directly as <code
            class="font-mono text-foreground">og:image</code
          >, make sure the image endpoint allows public access.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</MainLayout>
